Relevant columns, their potential usage and likely conditions
-------------------------------------------------------------
bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary  
• `country_region`  : filter to the seven requested countries.  
• `date`            : filter to the single day ‘2020‑04‑20’.  
• `confirmed`       : sum across all rows for each country (provinces / states) to obtain the national total.  

bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population  
• `country_name`    : filter to the same seven countries.  
• `indicator_code`  : keep only the World‑Bank total–population indicator ‘SP.POP.TOTL’.  
• `year`            : filter to 2020.  
• `value`           : add up (they are usually one row per country, but SUM() is safest) to obtain the 2020 population.  

Typical filter conditions that will be used  
```
WHERE date = DATE '2020-04-20'
      AND country_region IN ('United States', 'France', 'China', 'Italy', 'Spain', 'Germany', 'Iran')

WHERE year = 2020
      AND indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
      AND country_name IN ('United States', 'France', 'China', 'Italy', 'Spain', 'Germany', 'Iran')
```

Ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries
------------------------------------

```sql
-- Description: 1) Look at raw COVID‑19 rows for the United States on 20‑Apr‑2020.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
WHERE date = DATE '2020-04-20'
  AND country_region = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 2) List the distinct dates present in the COVID table (quick sanity check).
SELECT DISTINCT date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
ORDER BY date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 3) Display the distinct spellings of the seven target countries in the COVID table.
SELECT DISTINCT country_region
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
WHERE LOWER(country_region) IN ('us','france','china','italy','spain','germany','iran')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 4) Aggregate confirmed cases for the seven countries on 20‑Apr‑2020.
SELECT country_region,
       SUM(confirmed) AS total_confirmed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
WHERE date = DATE '2020-04-20'
  AND country_region IN ('US','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
GROUP BY country_region
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 5) Peek at 2020 World‑Bank indicators that contain “POP” to ensure the total‑population code exists.
SELECT DISTINCT indicator_code, indicator_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
WHERE year = 2020
  AND indicator_code LIKE '%POP%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 6) Grab the 2020 total‑population rows for the seven countries.
SELECT country_name,
       value AS population_2020
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
WHERE year = 2020
  AND indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
  AND country_name IN ('United States','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 7) Sum population values per country (defensive in case there are sub‑national rows).
SELECT country_name,
       SUM(value) AS population_2020
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
WHERE year = 2020
  AND indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
  AND country_name IN ('United States','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
GROUP BY country_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 8) Join COVID totals with 2020 population and compute cases per 100,000 people.
SELECT
  c.country_region            AS country,
  c.total_confirmed,
  p.population_2020,
  ROUND( (c.total_confirmed / p.population_2020) * 100000 , 2) AS cases_per_100k
FROM (
  SELECT country_region, SUM(confirmed) AS total_confirmed
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
  WHERE date = DATE '2020-04-20'
    AND country_region IN ('US','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
  GROUP BY country_region
) AS c
JOIN (
  SELECT country_name, SUM(value) AS population_2020
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
  WHERE year = 2020
    AND indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
    AND country_name IN ('United States','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
  GROUP BY country_name
) AS p
ON LOWER(c.country_region) = LOWER(p.country_name)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 9) Same as #8 but expressed with WITH‑clauses for readability.
WITH
  covid AS (
    SELECT country_region,
           SUM(confirmed) AS total_confirmed
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
    WHERE date = DATE '2020-04-20'
      AND country_region IN ('US','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
    GROUP BY country_region
  ),
  pop AS (
    SELECT country_name,
           SUM(value) AS population_2020
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
    WHERE year = 2020
      AND indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
      AND country_name IN ('United States','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
    GROUP BY country_name
  )
SELECT
  c.country_region AS country,
  c.total_confirmed,
  p.population_2020,
  ROUND((c.total_confirmed / p.population_2020) * 100000, 2) AS cases_per_100k
FROM covid c
JOIN pop   p ON LOWER(c.country_region) = LOWER(p.country_name)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 10) Final answer query (ready for production use).
SELECT
  CASE country_region
       WHEN 'US' THEN 'United States'
       ELSE country_region
  END                                        AS country,
  SUM(confirmed)                             AS total_confirmed,
  SUM(pop_2020)                              AS population_2020,
  ROUND( (SUM(confirmed) / SUM(pop_2020)) * 100000 , 2) AS cases_per_100k
FROM (
  SELECT s.country_region,
         s.confirmed,
         p.value AS pop_2020
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`        AS s
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population` AS p
    ON ( (s.country_region = 'US'  AND p.country_name = 'United States')
          OR LOWER(s.country_region) = LOWER(p.country_name) )
  WHERE s.date = DATE '2020-04-20'
    AND s.country_region IN ('US','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
    AND p.year = 2020
    AND p.indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
) 
GROUP BY country
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries progress from quick data inspection to the fully joined computation that yields the requested totals and “cases per 100,000 people” figure for each of the seven countries.
